From e1085f81a3de75233d37b33b6b6604658f00a7a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:23:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] hub admission: create reports the denied card's pool
 placement, not the pre-judge marker

`hermes kanban create --json` on the hub printed
`placement: {where: local, why: "home gateway marker: mentions '~/.hermes/l'"}` for a card
the admission judge had denied and queued for pool:worker + capability:hub-write
(self-heal t_01a1cfae6c9413c8, defect agent-aaab0fddf3). Agents read `where: local` /
`runs_where: here` as a hub pin and re-placed the card by hand.

- kanban_hub_admission_placement.denied_placement: one report for a denied card built from
  its persisted route: where=pool, runs_on or placement_policy, why naming the verdict, the
  verdict itself, and a "runs on ..., not on the hub; do not re-place it" note.
- CLI: cli_create_fields records the persisted (normalized) route on the plan; cli_report
  replaces the marker diagnostic for a denied card (JSON + human output, which now prints the
  note); an admitted card keeps its local report unchanged.
- kanban_create tool: placement/note come from the task row's runs_on (when the board has
  that column) and placement_policy for a denied card; runs_where says "worker pool: ..."
  for a denied queued card.

Test: tests/test_kanban_hub_admission_create_report.py (hub origin, fake judge deny,
~/.hermes/logs body; Board primary queue, non-primary and unsynced worker-first; admitted
controls for CLI and tool).
---
